    "created_at": "2025-01-30T07:33:16Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-01-30T07:57:27Z",
    "body": "The above test case only sets cookies with `document.cookie`. This currently causes infinite looping in Chrome and Safari--but not Mozilla. \n\nIf we change the case to set cookies with the Cookie Store API, Mozilla also loops infinitely:\n\n`cookieStore.addEventListener('change', (b) => {`\n`       cookieStore.set(\"hello\", \"there\");`\n`       console.log('change');`\n`});`\n`document.cookie='a=b';`\n\nCould any Mozilla folk explain why they fixed this only in the `document.cookie` change?\n\nAlso, I think the spec should enforce preventing this in both cases.\n\nThis would mean that if setting a cookie that already exists, we would not fire an event (unless I'm missing some edge case, this does make logical sense--it's a \"change\" event handler after all):\n\n`// event listener exists`\n`await cookieStore.set(\"name\", \"value\");    // event fires`\n`await cookieStore.set(\"name\", \"value\");    // event DOES NOT fire`\n\nWhat do we think?",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
